aura_node::baseline is a measurement, not a stub: it surveys the thirteen
library layers (files, lines, public item declarations) and classifies each as
implemented / placeholder / missing, and it lists the nine node capabilities
that do not exist with the phase that owes each.

- aurad refuses: no arguments -> exit 2 naming every missing capability and its
  phase; --config/--chain-id/--data-dir/--rpc-addr/--validator-key recognised
  and refused the same way; unknown command -> exit 64; report measures the tree
  and exits 3 when there is no workspace; --version says D0 baseline.
- Measured: 9 layers implemented, 4 placeholders (aura-consensus B1, aura-p2p
  N1, aura-mempool D3, aura-rpc D4 declare no public item), 0 missing.
- tools/gen_d0_vectors.py pins the survey in tests/fixtures/d0_baseline.txt from
  the binary's own report --fixture output; the gate compares live vs pin, so
  landing consensus code without moving the plan fails the build.
- tools/nc_d0.py: 6 negative controls, each reddening a named test after a green
  baseline. 15 tests in the gate, 374 in the workspace, 165 NC, 4857 vectors
  across 27 fixtures, 239 external crates unchanged — no new crate, no new
  dependency.
- Docs: docs/NODE.md, NODE_PLAN D0 receipt, STATUS, CHANGELOG, README, ROADMAP,
  CI (X0-X8 + D0, 165 NC).
